<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Standard SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> This SCP is a garden center of an abandoned hardware store. Containment is a faux construction site around the garden center. While external measurements only read 100 meters by 150 meters, measurements from the inside put it at 1.5 kilometers by 2 kilometers. The garden center is always full of plants, which change depending on the season. In spring, flowers are found throughout the center. In Summer vegetables are found In Fall, pumpkins and gourds are found. In Winter, Evergreen trees are found. Besides normal plants, unknown and anomalous varieties have been found. Inside the garden center, humanoid creatures roam the place. These creatures, while all distinctly human looking and having different physical features, all wear the employee uniform of the hardware store and will ask how they can help when approached. They are docile, but will attack an individual in self defense or if someone has damaged any of the plants inside.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The main narrative is of exploration and interacting with the humanoids inside the SCP.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> My concept is unique because it changes with the seasons. While somewhat similar to other SCP's with increased interior size and humanoids within, the space in my concept is finite, and the humanoids docile until attacked. Another unique part of my concept is the anomalous plants and unknown means of where the plants come from.</p>

